Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||02-10-2000||03:03 AM||||Anyone ever slam your Fiero door and crack the window glass?<P>I sometimes take my seatbelt off rather quickly in my mom's Taurus, and the seatbelt buckle smacks the window.. I don't usually slam the door, but one of these times the window will crack from the buckle, knowing my luck.. unless window glass is a lot stronger than I think it is.. which it probably is..<P>either way, anyone broken a Fiero window before?||||reg||1
Z||000001||BOILERMAKER||02-10-2000||07:49 AM||||Once that door window has a crack in it only a slight vibration will make the rest of the window shatter.  Once the first crack appears the window is very vulnerable.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||02-10-2000||09:33 AM||||The seat belt buckle would have to hit it pretty square and very hard to break the glass. <P>The tempered glass used for side and rear windows doesn't crack. If it does it won't be a crack long enough for you to see it before the whole thing beads up and falls on you. It will not crack or shard like "normal" glass used for residential windows. If a bucket of broken auto glass got spilled on you the worst youd get is a couple slivers. <P>This stuff is increadibly strong. That's why cars can use it in unframed door windows without much problem. <P>It will take some increadible impacts as long as they are at an angle. It will take some really big impacts square on as long as the area of impact is pretty large. Hit it square with something pointed tho and the stuff will break with some fairly small forces. It will also take major scratching without breaking. The properties of automotive safety glass are pretty strange when you compair it to "normal" glass.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||02-10-2000||07:58 PM||||My son got up too fast out of my passenger seat in the coupe I had a few years ago and hit his head on the windsheild and cracked it! Is sunroof glass made of the same glass as door glass or windsheild? ||||reg||1
