Z||000011||theogre||02-11-2000||10:00 AM||||Generally all auto window glass is tempered glass, including the roof glass. Only Windscreens are laminated glass.<P>The laminated glass is designed to break in a certain way. It is weaker if struck from inside. No, It doesn't like sudden cooling. (The tempered glass has also been known to let go when suddenly cooled.) The laminated glass when it does break is designed to have the plastic layer stretch at a certain rate. LAminated glass won't tollerate allot of things tempered will. You can't use it anyplace that doesn't fully support the glass perimiter. It would break in a day if used for the roof or door windows.||||reg||1
